<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad III of Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1093">1093</a>–<a href="/years/1152">1152</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad III was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1138 to 1152, the first ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen dynasty</a>. His election began the long rivalry between the Hohenstaufen and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a>. He led the German army on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>, which was mauled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in 1147 and failed before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 1148. He was never crowned emperor, and his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany.jpg" alt="Conrad III of Germany" width="320" height="708" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konrad_III_Miniatur_13_Jahrhundert.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
